messages:
ellie: opened a docs PR to add a migration guide for Private installs — moving customers from on-host PKCS#11 HSM to the HSM-proxy gateway. it has a port matrix, airgapped install steps, and a short JS SDK wrap/unwrap snippet. pls review when you can :wave:
rahul: can you post the PR link? and confirm smoke-test commands are in the PR body (ops requires conn checks for private/* changes).
ellie: PR is https://git.internal/redwood/docs/pull/2001. i put a checklist but still need to paste explicit commands (conn-check, http health). will add now.
pete: quick read: add NAT hairpin note for customers running proxy in same VPC/subnet as HSM. ports to call out: outbound TLS 443 (to cloud-hsm region) and local HSM tunnel TCP 15002. update port matrix please.
maya: minor infra note: older kernels (rhel7) exhibited bind failures when using SO_REUSEPORT. suggest a short sysctl block in the preflight: `net.core.somaxconn=1024` and call out `net.ipv4.tcp_tw_reuse=1` as a troubleshooting tip. also add `chronyc tracking` to airgap preflight for time sync.
ci-bot: PR 2001 updated by ellie — lint/docs: ok; linkcheck: 1 broken internal ref (/ops/hsm-proxy -> /ops/hsm-gateway).
ellie: thanks bot, fixing the link. adding the JS SDK example now: ```js
// wrap key example (client)
const Redwood = require('redwood');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
const plainKey = Buffer.from('customer-key-bytes');
const wrapped = await client.keys.wrap('migration:wrap', plainKey);
console.log(wrapped.toString('hex'));
```
rahul: add a tiny unwrap pseudo on the gateway side (3 lines) so integrators see server flow. also add a warning about keeping rotation windows small during migration — we once had a rotation happen mid-transfer and it caused failures.
pete: for airgapped installs expand steps to numbered checklist + checksum validation. include systemd dry-run snippet and sha256 example: `sha256sum redwood-proxy-bundle.tar.gz` + `sudo systemctl start redwood-proxy --no-block` (dry-run note).
maya: please also call out time sync before cert import (`chronyc tracking`) and suggest importing certs into system store rather than app-local store for easier ops.
ci-bot: reminder: docs PRs that touch private/* must include smoke test commands in the PR description.
ellie: added smoke test commands to the PR: `./bin/conn-check --target 127.0.0.1:15002` and `curl -sS http://127.0.0.1:15002/health`. added unwrap pseudo, rotation warning, sysctl tips, and chrony check. planning to merge after CI passes and a quick docs pass. please flag if you want wording changes. :tada:
